From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ive: reset the engine after a failed operation

An IVE operation that never completes (an unsupported image size, for
example) leaves the block stuck. Later two-input operations (SAD, Sub,
frame difference) then read their second image from a stale address and
return wrong results without any error, until the board restarts;
reloading the module does not help. Single-input operations are not
affected.

After a timeout, reset the IVE through its VIP reset bit, as the
reset ioctl already does, so the next operation starts clean.

diff --git a/interdrv/ive/hal/cv181x/cvi_ive_platform.c b/interdrv/ive/hal/cv181x/cvi_ive_platform.c
--- a/interdrv/ive/hal/cv181x/cvi_ive_platform.c
+++ b/interdrv/ive/hal/cv181x/cvi_ive_platform.c
@@ -1875,6 +1875,12 @@ inline CVI_S32 cvi_ive_go(struct cvi_ive_device *ndev, IVE_TOP_C *ive_top_c,
 		if (leavetime <= 0)
 			ret = CVI_FAILURE;
 	}
+	/* An operation that never finishes (an unsupported size, for example)
+	 * leaves the engine stuck: every later two-input operation then reads
+	 * its second image from a stale address. Reset the block so the next
+	 * operation starts clean. */
+	if (ret != CVI_SUCCESS)
+		cvi_ive_reset(ndev, 0);
 	if (ndev->tile_num == ndev->total_tile) {
 		complete(&ndev->op_done);
 	}
